Practical 1.2 – Finding Repeated Book IDs
1.2 :

a. I learned how to find the duplicate elements in an array by comparing each element with every other element and printing only the unique repeated values.

b. At first I was confused about how to avoid printing the same book ID multiple times because if an element appears more than twice, it can easily get printed again and again.

c. While implementing this program, I understood that checking whether an element has already been printed before displaying it helps in avoiding duplicate outputs. I also realized that this approach scans the array multiple times, so although it works correctly, it is not very efficient for a very large number of records. Using a hash map or frequency array can reduce the number of passes and improve the overall time complexity.
